From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:54:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: use the vendor hang-detect threshold

The interface hang threshold is in units of 16 GPU cycles. 0xFFFF is
about one million cycles -- 1.5 ms at the a540's top frequency -- short
enough that a single long but perfectly healthy draw trips fault
detection. Qualcomm's own driver has always used 0x3FFFF, four million
cycles, for every a5xx past a530v1. Use their number.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
index c7206606a18d..3f056ae2e96b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -803,9 +803,16 @@ static int a5xx_hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 			0xFFFFFFFF);
 	}
 
-	/* Enable fault detection */
+	/* Enable fault detection.
+	 *
+	 * The threshold is in units of 16 GPU cycles. 0xFFFF is about one
+	 * million cycles -- 1.5ms at the a540's top frequency -- which is
+	 * short enough that a single long but perfectly healthy draw trips
+	 * it. Qualcomm's own driver has always used 0x3FFFF here, four
+	 * million cycles, for every a5xx past a530v1. Use their number.
+	 */
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_RBBM_INTERFACE_HANG_INT_CNTL,
-		(1 << 30) | 0xFFFF);
+		(1 << 30) | 0x3FFFF);
 
 	/* Turn on performance counters */
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_RBBM_PERFCTR_CNTL, 0x01);
